507     {\cf20 // Parameters stacks (font)}\par
508     {\cf20 //  - PushFont(font, 0.0f)                       // Change font and keep current size}\par
509     {\cf20 //  - PushFont(NULL, 20.0f)                      // Keep font and change current size}\par
510     {\cf20 //  - PushFont(font, 20.0f)                      // Change font and set size to 20.0f}\par
511     {\cf20 //  - PushFont(font, style.FontSizeBase * 2.0f)  // Change font and set size to be twice bigger than current size.}\par
512     {\cf20 //  - PushFont(font, font->LegacySize)           // Change font and set size to size passed to AddFontXXX() function. Same as pre-1.92 behavior.}\par
513     {\cf20 // *IMPORTANT* before 1.92, fonts had a single size. They can now be dynamically be adjusted.}\par
514     {\cf20 //  - In 1.92 we have REMOVED the single parameter version of PushFont() because it seems like the easiest way to provide an error-proof transition.}\par
515     {\cf20 //  - PushFont(font) before 1.92 = PushFont(font, font->LegacySize) after 1.92          // Use default font size as passed to AddFontXXX() function.}\par
516     {\cf20 // *IMPORTANT* global scale factors are applied over the provided size.}\par
517     {\cf20 //  - Global scale factors are: 'style.FontScaleMain', 'style.FontScaleDpi' and maybe more.}\par
518     {\cf20 // -  If you want to apply a factor to the _current_ font size:}\par
519     {\cf20 //  - CORRECT:   PushFont(NULL, style.FontSizeBase)         // use current unscaled size    == does nothing}\par
520     {\cf20 //  - CORRECT:   PushFont(NULL, style.FontSizeBase * 2.0f)  // use current unscaled size x2 == make text twice bigger}\par
