2006 {\cf20 // Flags for ImGui::BeginTable()}\par
2007 {\cf20 // - Important! Sizing policies have complex and subtle side effects, much more so than you would expect.}\par
2008 {\cf20 //   Read comments/demos carefully + experiment with live demos to get acquainted with them.}\par
2009 {\cf20 // - The DEFAULT sizing policies are:}\par
2010 {\cf20 //    - Default to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingFixedFit    if ScrollX is on, or if host window has ImGuiWindowFlags_AlwaysAutoResize.}\par
2011 {\cf20 //    - Default to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingStretchSame if ScrollX is off.}\par
2012 {\cf20 // - When ScrollX is off:}\par
2013 {\cf20 //    - Table defaults to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingStretchSame -> all Columns defaults to ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthStretch with same weight.}\par
2014 {\cf20 //    - Columns sizing policy allowed: Stretch (default), Fixed/Auto.}\par
2015 {\cf20 //    - Fixed Columns (if any) will generally obtain their requested width (unless the table cannot fit them all).}\par
2016 {\cf20 //    - Stretch Columns will share the remaining width according to their respective weight.}\par
2017 {\cf20 //    - Mixed Fixed/Stretch columns is possible but has various side-effects on resizing behaviors.}\par
2018 {\cf20 //      The typical use of mixing sizing policies is: any number of LEADING Fixed columns, followed by one or two TRAILING Stretch columns.}\par
2019 {\cf20 //      (this is because the visible order of columns have subtle but necessary effects on how they react to manual resizing).}\par
2020 {\cf20 // - When ScrollX is on:}\par
2021 {\cf20 //    - Table defaults to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingFixedFit -> all Columns defaults to ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthFixed}\par
2022 {\cf20 //    - Columns sizing policy allowed: Fixed/Auto mostly.}\par
2023 {\cf20 //    - Fixed Columns can be enlarged as needed. Table will show a horizontal scrollbar if needed.}\par
2024 {\cf20 //    - When using auto-resizing (non-resizable) fixed columns, querying the content width to use item right-alignment e.g. SetNextItemWidth(-FLT_MIN) doesn't make sense, would create a feedback loop.}\par
2025 {\cf20 //    - Using Stretch columns OFTEN DOES NOT MAKE SENSE if ScrollX is on, UNLESS you have specified a value for 'inner_width' in BeginTable().}\par
2026 {\cf20 //      If you specify a value for 'inner_width' then effectively the scrolling space is known and Stretch or mixed Fixed/Stretch columns become meaningful again.}\par
2027 {\cf20 // - Read on documentation at the top of imgui_tables.cpp for details.}\par
2028 {\cf17 enum} ImGuiTableFlags_\par
2029 \{\par
2030     {\cf20 // Features}\par
2031     ImGuiTableFlags_None                       = 0,\par
2032     ImGuiTableFlags_Resizable                  = 1 << 0,   {\cf20 // Enable resizing columns.}\par
2033     ImGuiTableFlags_Reorderable                = 1 << 1,   {\cf20 // Enable reordering columns in header row (need calling TableSetupColumn() + TableHeadersRow() to display headers)}\par
2034     ImGuiTableFlags_Hideable                   = 1 << 2,   {\cf20 // Enable hiding/disabling columns in context menu.}\par
2035     ImGuiTableFlags_Sortable                   = 1 << 3,   {\cf20 // Enable sorting. Call TableGetSortSpecs() to obtain sort specs. Also see ImGuiTableFlags_SortMulti and ImGuiTableFlags_SortTristate.}\par
2036     ImGuiTableFlags_NoSavedSettings            = 1 << 4,   {\cf20 // Disable persisting columns order, width, visibility and sort settings in the .ini file.}\par
2037     ImGuiTableFlags_ContextMenuInBody          = 1 << 5,   {\cf20 // Right-click on columns body/contents will display table context menu. By default it is available in TableHeadersRow().}\par
2038     {\cf20 // Decorations}\par
