2125 {\cf20 // Enum for ImGui::TableSetBgColor()}\par
2126 {\cf20 // Background colors are rendering in 3 layers:}\par
2127 {\cf20 //  - Layer 0: draw with RowBg0 color if set, otherwise draw with ColumnBg0 if set.}\par
2128 {\cf20 //  - Layer 1: draw with RowBg1 color if set, otherwise draw with ColumnBg1 if set.}\par
2129 {\cf20 //  - Layer 2: draw with CellBg color if set.}\par
2130 {\cf20 // The purpose of the two row/columns layers is to let you decide if a background color change should override or blend with the existing color.}\par
2131 {\cf20 // When using ImGuiTableFlags_RowBg on the table, each row has the RowBg0 color automatically set for odd/even rows.}\par
2132 {\cf20 // If you set the color of RowBg0 target, your color will override the existing RowBg0 color.}\par
2133 {\cf20 // If you set the color of RowBg1 or ColumnBg1 target, your color will blend over the RowBg0 color.}\par
