3644 {\cf20 // Load and rasterize multiple TTF/OTF fonts into a same texture. The font atlas will build a single texture holding:}\par
3645 {\cf20 //  - One or more fonts.}\par
3646 {\cf20 //  - Custom graphics data needed to render the shapes needed by Dear ImGui.}\par
3647 {\cf20 //  - Mouse cursor shapes for software cursor rendering (unless setting 'Flags |= ImFontAtlasFlags_NoMouseCursors' in the font atlas).}\par
3648 {\cf20 //  - If you don't call any AddFont*** functions, the default font embedded in the code will be loaded for you.}\par
3649 {\cf20 // It is the rendering backend responsibility to upload texture into your graphics API:}\par
3650 {\cf20 //  - ImGui_ImplXXXX_RenderDrawData() functions generally iterate platform_io->Textures[] to create/update/destroy each ImTextureData instance.}\par
3651 {\cf20 //  - Backend then set ImTextureData's TexID and BackendUserData.}\par
3652 {\cf20 //  - Texture id are passed back to you during rendering to identify the texture. Read FAQ entry about ImTextureID/ImTextureRef for more details.}\par
3653 {\cf20 // Legacy path:}\par
3654 {\cf20 //  - Call Build() + GetTexDataAsAlpha8() or GetTexDataAsRGBA32() to build and retrieve pixels data.}\par
3655 {\cf20 //  - Call SetTexID(my_tex_id); and pass the pointer/identifier to your texture in a format natural to your graphics API.}\par
3656 {\cf20 // Common pitfalls:}\par
3657 {\cf20 // - If you pass a 'glyph_ranges' array to AddFont*** functions, you need to make sure that your array persists up until the}\par
3658 {\cf20 //   atlas is build (when calling GetTexData*** or Build()). We only copy the pointer, not the data.}\par
3659 {\cf20 // - Important: By default, AddFontFromMemoryTTF() takes ownership of the data. Even though we are not writing to it, we will free the pointer on destruction.}\par
3660 {\cf20 //   You can set font_cfg->FontDataOwnedByAtlas=false to keep ownership of your data and it won't be freed,}\par
3661 {\cf20 // - Even though many functions are suffixed with "TTF", OTF data is supported just as well.}\par
3662 {\cf20 // - This is an old API and it is currently awkward for those and various other reasons! We will address them in the future!}\par
3663 {\cf17 struct }ImFontAtlas\par
3664 \{\par
