3728     {\cf20 // Register and retrieve custom rectangles}\par
3729     {\cf20 // - You can request arbitrary rectangles to be packed into the atlas, for your own purpose.}\par
3730     {\cf20 // - Since 1.92.0, packing is done immediately in the function call (previously packing was done during the Build call)}\par
3731     {\cf20 // - You can render your pixels into the texture right after calling the AddCustomRect() functions.}\par
3732     {\cf20 // - VERY IMPORTANT:}\par
3733     {\cf20 //   - Texture may be created/resized at any time when calling ImGui or ImFontAtlas functions.}\par
3734     {\cf20 //   - IT WILL INVALIDATE RECTANGLE DATA SUCH AS UV COORDINATES. Always use latest values from GetCustomRect().}\par
3735     {\cf20 //   - UV coordinates are associated to the current texture identifier aka 'atlas->TexRef'. Both TexRef and UV coordinates are typically changed at the same time.}\par
3736     {\cf20 // - If you render colored output into your custom rectangles: set 'atlas->TexPixelsUseColors = true' as this may help some backends decide of preferred texture format.}\par
3737     {\cf20 // - Read docs/FONTS.md for more details about using colorful icons.}\par
3738     {\cf20 // - Note: this API may be reworked further in order to facilitate supporting e.g. multi-monitor, varying DPI settings.}\par
3739     {\cf20 // - (Pre-1.92 names) ------------> (1.92 names)}\par
3740     {\cf20 //   - GetCustomRectByIndex()   --> Use GetCustomRect()}\par
3741     {\cf20 //   - CalcCustomRectUV()       --> Use GetCustomRect() and read uv0, uv1 fields.}\par
3742     {\cf20 //   - AddCustomRectRegular()   --> Renamed to AddCustomRect()}\par
3743     {\cf20 //   - AddCustomRectFontGlyph() --> Prefer using custom ImFontLoader inside ImFontConfig}\par
3744     {\cf20 //   - ImFontAtlasCustomRect    --> Renamed to ImFontAtlasRect}\par
3745     IMGUI_API ImFontAtlasRectId AddCustomRect({\cf18 int} width, {\cf18 int} height, ImFontAtlasRect* out_r = NULL);{\cf20 // Register a rectangle. Return -1 (ImFontAtlasRectId_Invalid) on error.}\par
